<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a translation</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Achieng translated triangle PQR by the vector \(\mathbf{T} = {@col(T)@}\). The vertices are \(P({@O[1][1]@},\,{@O[1][2]@})\), \(Q({@O[2][1]@},\,{@O[2][2]@})\) and \(R({@O[3][1]@},\,{@O[3][2]@})\). She wrote the images as \(P'({@shown[1][1]@},\,{@shown[1][2]@})\), \(Q'({@shown[2][1]@},\,{@shown[2][2]@})\) and \(R'({@shown[3][1]@},\,{@shown[3][2]@})\). One of her images is wrong.</p><p>(a) Which image is wrong?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Give the correct coordinates of that image.</p><div>( [[input:ans2]] , [[input:ans3]] ) [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]]</div><div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Add \(\mathbf{T}\) to every vertex and compare with Achieng's points.</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Vertex</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Coordinates</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Vertex + T</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Achieng's image</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;"></th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">P</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@O[1][1]@},\,{@O[1][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@good[1][1]@},\,{@good[1][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@shown[1][1]@},\,{@shown[1][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(w=1)"]]wrong[[else]]right[[/if]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Q</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@O[2][1]@},\,{@O[2][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@good[2][1]@},\,{@good[2][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@shown[2][1]@},\,{@shown[2][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(w=2)"]]wrong[[else]]right[[/if]]</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">R</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@O[3][1]@},\,{@O[3][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@good[3][1]@},\,{@good[3][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(({@shown[3][1]@},\,{@shown[3][2]@})\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(w=3)"]]wrong[[else]]right[[/if]]</td></tr></table><p>(a) [[if test="is(w=1)"]]P'[[/if]][[if test="is(w=2)"]]Q'[[/if]][[if test="is(w=3)"]]R'[[/if]] is wrong. [[if test="is(er=1)"]]She swapped the two components of \(\mathbf{T}\) at that vertex.[[/if]][[if test="is(er=2)"]]She subtracted \(\mathbf{T}\) at that vertex instead of adding it.[[/if]][[if test="is(er=3)"]]She changed the sign of the move up at that vertex.[[/if]]</p><p>(b) The correct image is \(({@xx@},\,{@yy@})\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: find what is wrong with a claimed translation. Entries [triangle, T, w = the wrong vertex, er]; er 1 swapped the components of T at that vertex, er 2 subtracted T, er 3 changed the sign of the y-move. w counts 3, 4, 3; er counts 4, 3, 3. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Foundation 2, Chapter 15, Section B, B3. */
L: [[[[1,-4],[4,-4],[1,-2]],[-4,5],1,1],[[[2,-1],[5,-1],[2,1]],[-2,-5],1,2],[[[2,2],[6,2],[3,4]],[3,-6],1,3],[[[-2,3],[0,2],[1,5]],[1,-5],2,1],[[[-1,3],[1,3],[1,6]],[4,3],2,2],[[[0,2],[2,2],[2,5]],[-3,2],2,3],[[[1,0],[5,0],[2,2]],[-2,-5],2,1],[[[3,3],[5,3],[5,6]],[-3,1],3,1],[[[2,0],[5,0],[2,2]],[1,6],3,2],[[[0,2],[2,2],[2,5]],[-1,2],3,3]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
O: L[ix][1]; T: L[ix][2]; w: L[ix][3]; er: L[ix][4];
good: [O[1]+T, O[2]+T, O[3]+T];
bad: if er=1 then O[w]+[T[2],T[1]] elseif er=2 then O[w]-T else O[w]+[T[1],-T[2]];
shown: makelist(if jj=w then bad else good[jj], jj, 1, 3);
xx: good[w][1]; yy: good[w][2];
Ow: O[w];
wo: mod(w,3)+1; oth: good[wo];
opt1: [["allok", false, "None: all three are right"], ["pp", is(w=1), "P'"], ["qq", is(w=2), "Q'"], ["rr", is(w=3), "R'"]];
ta1: first(mcq_correct(opt1)); wrong1: ["pp","qq","rr"][wo];
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
